{"id":"incline_treadmill_walk","name":"Incline treadmill walk","cue":"Easy pace, tall posture, hands free.","research":"Walking on a treadmill at a 10 percent incline (5.7 deg), the easy-cardio swap for the bike (science audit table B). Cycle mode: the crank angle is the stride phase (0 = left heel strike), 1.1 s per stride (about 110 steps a minute), two strides per loop, belt 3.8 km/h (stride 0.66 H = 1.2 m). Gait events as in level walking (Winter): heel strike 0, foot flat 8 percent, heel off 40 percent, toe off 60 percent of the stride; the right side runs 180 deg behind. The stance foot is carried by a chain of two slides and a hinge on the belt direction (parts fb/fc/fh/fa): a baseline slide moves it back at exactly the belt speed (so the foot never slides on the belt), keyed corrections roll the foot over the heel (heel strike) and the ball (heel off), and the swing foot follows a Hermite path with the belt speed at both ends and 5 cm of toe clearance; foot IK with plate alignment sets the sole pitch (pitch +14 deg at heel strike, -34 deg at toe off, relative to the belt). The pelvis hangs from a socket that rides the lower of the two legs reach (bob 0.02 H, knees 10-15 deg in stance), the trunk leans 9 deg (spinal flexion 4), the pelvis turns 3.5 deg with the swinging leg and the thorax counter-turns, arms swing opposite the legs (shoulder -18 to +10, elbow 23-41). Read-back ranges: hip -2 to 45, knee 9 to 61, ankle -7 to 24, hip abduction 0-2. The treadmill: a belt deck tilted 5.7 deg on two legs and a front motor housing, an upright console arch with short handrails in front of the hands (the arms swing free). Glute and quad glow as the bike (activation peaks at loading response). The belt is a solid part: the skin check shows no penetration at any phase and the soles lie on the belt (gap 0.001 H) through the flat-foot phases.","targets":{"tol":10,"note":"Cycle mode: the leg angles are checked as loop extremes (R). Trunk lean and arm carriage are constant per frame and checked by A/B.","A":{"trunk_flexion":9},"B":{"trunk_flexion":9},"R":{"knee_flexion":[[3,16],[54,68]],"hip_flexion":[[-9,5],[38,52]],"ankle_dorsiflexion":[[-14,0],[16,30]]}},"muscles":{"primary":["vast_lat","vast_med","glute_max"],"secondary":[],"side":"both"},"camera":{"az":90,"el":5,"dAz":0,"dEl":0,"fill":0.58,"note":"Research view of the bike (az 90, el 5: the right profile, so the stride, the trunk lean and the heel-to-toe roll read side-on). The belt runs off the left of the frame and the console stands at the right, in front of the figure; the deck stands on two legs and cross feet so the floor under the name stays clear. fitMachine: the deck, the console and the handrails stay in the frame (the front of the machine was cropped at the right edge).","fitMachine":true},"rhythm":false,"motion":{"mode":"cycle","period":1.1,"revs":2,"dof":"crank","offset":0,"bind":0.1,"root":[0,0.588640690857075,0],"base":{"pelvis":{"flex":5},"lumbar":{"flex":2},"thorax":{"flex":2},"neck":{"flex":-2},"head":{"flex":-3},"thigh_l":{"flex":20,"abd":1},"shank_l":{"flex":10},"clav_l":{"elev":0,"pro":0},"arm_l":{"plane":90,"elev":0,"rot":90},"fore_l":{"flex":30},"hand_l":{"pro":90}},"keys":{"A":{}},"crankPose":[{"deg":0,"pose":{"m":{"fc_l":-0.01003,"fh_l":0.00368,"fa_l":14,"fc_r":0.0154,"fh_r":0.02094,"fa_r":-17.68902,"hy":0},"pelvis":{"rot":3.5},"thorax":{"rot":-4.2},"toe_l":{"ext":0},"arm_l":{"elev":10},"fore_l":{"flex":32}}},{"deg":10,"pose":{"m":{"fc_l":-0.00748,"fh_l":0.003,"fa_l":10.55092,"fc_r":0.02276,"fh_r":0.02746,"fa_r":-24.35773,"hy":0.00433},"pelvis":{"rot":3.44683},"thorax":{"rot":-4.13619},"toe_l":{"ext":0},"arm_l":{"elev":9.78731},"fore_l":{"flex":33.56283}}},{"deg":20,"pose":{"m":{"fc_l":-0.00139,"fh_l":0.00068,"fa_l":2.02582,"fc_r":0.02945,"fh_r":0.03221,"fa_r":-29.9189,"hy":0.0054},"pelvis":{"rot":3.28892},"thorax":{"rot":-3.94671},"toe_l":{"ext":0},"arm_l":{"elev":9.1557},"fore_l":{"flex":35.07818}}},{"deg":30,"pose":{"m":{"fc_l":0,"fh_l":0,"fa_l":0,"fc